# Accepted Trivy findings (R4-1). Each entry: why it is accepted, what removes it, and an expiry
# date after which the scan fails again. Fix instead of ignoring whenever a fix exists.

# zlib1g in python:3.12-slim (Debian 13; api and the MCP servers): gz_vacate() heap overflow.
# Debian ships 1:1.3.dfsg+really1.3.1-1+deb13u1, but the official python:3.12-slim image does not
# have it yet (checked 2026-11-19). Removed by the next rebuild of the base image.
CVE-2026-85091 exp:2026-12-19

# filelock 3.32.7 in the api (through litellm and huggingface-hub): only ReadWriteLock is affected,
# and nothing in the api or its packages uses it (checked 2026-11-19). The fix (4.2.1) is outside
# litellm 1.108.1's `filelock<4`; litellm 1.110.1 allows it, and that upgrade (ADR-004) removes this.
CVE-2026-112940 exp:2026-12-19
